    "result_text": "The build succeeds and all tests pass. The audit log confirms consistent behavior: a registration date of `2026-09-21` (September, on/after 1 July) yields fiscal year FY27 and membership number `...-M27`.\n\n## Summary\n\nMoved all date-derived values onto a fiscal-year basis (fiscal year starts 1 July, named by the year it ends in \u2014 e.g. 1 Jul 2025\u201330 Jun 2026 = FY26).\n\n**New `FiscalYear` value type** (`model/FiscalYear.java`) \u2014 a single small unit owning the fiscal-year derivation, reused everywhere:\n- `of(LocalDate)` \u2014 maps a date to its fiscal year (calendar year, +1 when the month is July or later).\n- `getShortYear()` / `getLabel()` \u2014 the two-digit year and the `FY<YY>` label.\n- `yearsUntil(other)` \u2014 elapsed whole fiscal years, for tenure.\n\n**Wired it into the three date-derived behaviours:**\n1. **`fiscalYear` field** \u2014 added `Owner.getFiscalYear()` (returns `FY<YY>` from the business-day-adjusted `registrationDate`, `null` when absent) plus the `fiscalYear` property in the OpenAPI `Owner` schema, so MapStruct maps it onto the DTO automatically.\n2. **Membership identifier year segment** \u2014 `MembershipNumberGenerator` now takes the suffix from the registration date's fiscal year instead of its calendar year.\n3. **Tenure** \u2014 `Owner.hasQualifyingTenure()` now counts *elapsed fiscal years* (more than 1) between registration and today, replacing the 365-day window. Removed the now-unused `ChronoUnit` import.\n\nJavadoc and the OpenAPI descriptions for `membershipNumber`, `membershipPoints`, and the new `fiscalYear` were updated to match. Each piece of logic stayed in its existing home; nothing was duplicated \u2014 the fiscal-year rule lives in one class.",
